decision: pass
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: Where does the contract format live canonically, and how far does the sh check approximate it?

Records that JSON Schema is the source of truth for the contract format and that the sh `engsys check` is an approximation over required fields and top-level keys.
Translated from Korean to English; frontmatter, paths (schemas/*.json, tests/test-schema.sh, tools/lib/jsonschema_min.py), the ADR 0001 link and the fail-on-unimplemented-keyword rule are unchanged.
Headings mapped to Context, Decision, Alternatives and Consequences; bold emphasis kept on the same terms as the source.
The stated limitation (no equivalence over all inputs; hand-edited detail outside top-level keys is missed) is preserved.
No Korean literals retained.

